@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `hvac-nouns`
IMPORT `hvac-law-s63-commencement`
IMPORT `hvac-law-s8-validity`

-- hvac-law-s2-s3-licensing-duty.l4 -- Law s 2 (the definitions the rules turn on) and s 3
-- (the duty to hold a licence).  Quoted from Hebrew Wikisource rev 2947808 (unofficial);
-- checked by eye against the gazette (Sefer HaChukim 3349 pp 182-183).
--
-- The First Schedule (which acts need which licence) is OUTSIDE the pinned scope and is not
-- encoded.  What s 3 needs from it arrives as two facts on the piece of work: that the act is
-- one the First Schedule fixes, and that it is one reserved to Grade 3 (Part B item 3(2) and
-- (3)).  Nor are the Fourth Schedule, ss 4-5 and 10-15, 18-62 or the Third Schedule encoded.

§ `Section 2: Definitions`

-- The definitions that carry rules.  The others -- "אגף להכשרה מקצועית" (the Vocational
-- Training Division), "בעל רישיון" (licensee), the cross-references to the Technicians Act, the
-- Electricity Law and the Penal Law, "המועצה" (the Council), "מפקח" and "המפקח הבכיר" (inspector
-- and senior inspector), "מרשם ההנדסאים והטכנאים המוסמכים", "המשרד" (the Ministry), "קרר"
-- (refrigerant), "הרשם" (the Registrar) and "השר" (the Minister) -- name an office, a statute
-- or a thing, and are inert: they are the nouns of hvac-nouns.l4, not rules.

-- "מערכת קירור או מיזוג אוויר", "מערכת":
@@Q law 48@@
@ref Law s 2, "מערכת קירור או מיזוג אוויר"
GIVEN sys IS A `Refrigeration or air-conditioning system`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2: this is a refrigeration or air-conditioning system` sys MEANS
        sys's `its purpose is the removal of heat to the outside of a given substance or space`
    AND sys's `it removes heat by means of a refrigerant`

-- "עבודה במערכת קירור או מיזוג אוויר":
@@Q law 53@@
@ref Law s 2, "עבודה במערכת קירור או מיזוג אוויר"
GIVEN w IS A `Piece of work`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2: this is work on a refrigeration or air-conditioning system` w MEANS
        `s 2: this is a refrigeration or air-conditioning system` (w's `the system worked on`)
    AND w's `the act is of a type fixed in the First Schedule`

-- The three grades, by what they cover:
@@Q law 55 59 60 61@@
@ref Law s 2, "רישיון דרגה 1", "רישיון דרגה 2", "רישיון דרגה 3"
GIVEN g  IS A `Licence grade`
      kw IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2: a licence of` g `covers work on a system of cooling output` kw `kilowatts` MEANS
    CONSIDER g
    WHEN `Grade 1` THEN kw AT MOST 18
    WHEN `Grade 2` THEN kw AT MOST 70
    WHEN `Grade 3` THEN TRUE

-- "תעודת גמר" -- a final certificate is one of two things.  Paragraph (1) is the one the
-- SimpLEX worked example reaches for when it says the Law "requires passing an exam": a
-- Division certificate counts only if its holder passed an exam that included BOTH a theory
-- exam and a practical exam.
@@Q law 63 64 65@@
@ref Law s 2, "תעודת גמר" paragraphs (1) and (2)
GIVEN c IS A Certificate
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2: this is a final certificate` c MEANS
        (  "(1)" ... c's `issued by the Division`
                 AND c's `it attests completion of refrigeration and air-conditioning studies`
                 AND c's `it attests successful passing of an exam held by the Division`
                 AND c's `the exam held by the Division included a theory exam`
                 AND c's `the exam held by the Division included a practical exam`)
    OR  (  "(2)" ... c's `issued by the Ministry of Education`
                 AND c's `it attests successful completion of studies in the climate-control track`)

§ `Section 3: The duty to hold a licence`

@@Q law 71 72 73@@

-- s 3(a): "רישיון מהסוג המתאים לביצוע עבודה באותה מערכת כמפורט בטור א' בתוספת הראשונה".  A licence
-- is of the appropriate type when its grade covers the system's cooling output (s 2) and, for
-- an act the First Schedule reserves to Grade 3, the grade is Grade 3.
@ref Law s 3(a); s 2; First Schedule (not encoded) Part B item 3(2) and (3)
GIVEN g IS A `Licence grade`
      w IS A `Piece of work`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 3(a): a licence of` g `is of a type appropriate to` w MEANS
        `s 2: a licence of` g `covers work on a system of cooling output` (w's `the system worked on`'s `cooling output in kilowatts`) `kilowatts`
    AND (   NOT w's `the act is reserved to Grade 3 by Part B item 3(2) or (3) of the First Schedule`
         OR g EQUALS `Grade 3`)

-- When is a licence required at all?  For work on a system that s 2 defines, unless the
-- Minister has exempted the type of system by order under s 3(b) -- an order is a fact the
-- caller supplies; none is in the sources -- and only once the Law is in force for work on a
-- system with that refrigerant (s 63).  Before that the Law has nothing to say, and that is an
-- ordinary answer.
@ref Law s 3(a), (b); s 63
GIVEN w IS A `Piece of work`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 3(a): a licence is required for` w MEANS
        `s 2: this is work on a refrigeration or air-conditioning system` w
    AND NOT w's `a Minister's order under section 3(b) exempts this type of system`
    AND `the Law is in force on` (w's `the date of the work`) `for work on a system using` (w's `the system worked on`'s `refrigerant`)

-- Does the person hold a licence that is valid on the day of the work and of the appropriate
-- type?  A temporary licence for a foreign expert (s 9) is a Grade 3 licence.
@ref Law s 3(a); s 8
GIVEN w IS A `Piece of work`
      x IS A `Person doing work`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 3(a): the person holds a valid licence of the appropriate type for` w `, being` x MEANS
    CONSIDER x's `the licence held`
    WHEN NOTHING  THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST l   THEN
            `the licence` l `is valid on` (w's `the date of the work`)
        AND `s 3(a): a licence of` (l's `grade`) `is of a type appropriate to` w

-- The prohibition is met when no licence is required, or when the person holds a valid
-- licence of the appropriate type AND acts in accordance with its conditions and the Law
-- ("ובהתאם לתנאי רישיונו ולהוראות לפי חוק זה").  s 17(d) makes the refresher-training duty one of
-- those conditions (see hvac-law-s17-refresher-training.l4).
@ref Law s 3(a)
GIVEN x IS A `Person doing work`
      w IS A `Piece of work`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 3(a): the prohibition is complied with by` x `in` w MEANS
        NOT `s 3(a): a licence is required for` w
    OR  (       `s 3(a): the person holds a valid licence of the appropriate type for` w `, being` x
            AND x's `acting in accordance with the conditions of the licence and the Law`)

-- The same prohibition as a rule of conduct: where a licence is required and the person does
-- not hold one of the appropriate type, doing the work is the breach.  No WITHIN: the prohibition
-- holds for as long as the facts do.  The sanction (Chapter 6, Third Schedule items 1 and 2) is
-- outside the pinned scope.
@ref Law s 3(a): "לא יבצע אדם עבודה ... אלא אם כן בידו רישיון"
GIVEN x IS A `Person doing work`
      w IS A `Piece of work`
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party under the Law` `Act under the Law`
`s 3(a): the person must not perform the work` x `in` w MEANS
    IF       `s 3(a): a licence is required for` w
         AND NOT `s 3(a): the person holds a valid licence of the appropriate type for` w `, being` x
    THEN PARTY `the person doing the work`
         SHANT `perform work on the system`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST  BREACH BY `the person doing the work`
               BECAUSE "s 3(a): work on a system was performed without a valid licence of the appropriate type"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- s 3(b) is the Minister's power to exempt types of system by order, after consulting the
-- Council; s 3(c) is his power, with the approval of the Knesset Labour and Welfare Committee,
-- to amend the First Schedule.  The first is represented by the fact on the piece of work (an
-- order made is a fact the caller supplies); the second is inert.  Whether any order has been
-- made the sources do not say.
